ssh-keys-disk"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_shintoist", "story_50609579", "front_page"], "author": "shintoist", "children": [50613505, 50613802, 50613839, 50613931, 50613946, 50614131, 50614266, 50614530, 50614636, 50614750, 50615054, 50615108, 50615220, 50615527, 50615890, 50616453, 50616524, 50617037], "created_at": "2026-11-23T09:55:38Z", "created_at_i": 1795427738, "num_comments": 59, "objectID": "50609579", "points": 73, "story_id": 50609579, "title": "Don't keep your SSH keys on disk", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:57:19Z", "url": "https://jola.dev/posts/you-cant-afford-ssh-keys-disk"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "johnwards"}, "story_text": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "So this started out just over a week ago, could I drive around my village in my old car on the web, and its expanded into a massive map, with races, events, different cars and multiplayer.<p>I'm a web/app guy, backend guy, and yes I build it with Claude.<p>I know I shouldn't be astounded by what these Ai agents can do as of today, but here I am still amazed.<p>I've even got support from a Sim racing guy and built a web driver so he gets full force feedback for his rig, and it works.<p>Anyway, just a bit of fun!<p>Uses LIDAR data from the UK Gov + OpenStreetMap data to build the world. Technically, I could do the whole of England/Wales...but the data storage would be huge!"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: Drive around my village in 3D"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://cherwellvalleymotorclub.app"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_johnwards", "story_50574412", "show_hn", "front_page"], "author": "johnwards", "children": [50574566, 50577286, 50579614, 50580184, 50583634, 50584210, 50609441, 50609501, 50609502, 50609630, 50609779, 50609907, 50609912, 50609959, 50610107, 50610129, 50610253, 50610270, 50610284, 50610574, 50610609, 50610753, 50610826, 50611503, 50611632, 50614010, 50616430, 50616640, 50616709, 50616782, 50616835], "created_at": "2026-11-20T13:32:42Z", "created_at_i": 1795181562, "num_comments": 50, "objectID": "50574412", "points": 66, "story_id": 50574412, "story_text": "So this started out just over a week ago, could I drive around my village in my old car on the web, and its expanded into a massive map, with races, events, different cars and multiplayer.<p>I&#x27;m a web&#x2F;app guy, backend guy, and yes I build it with Claude.<p>I know I shouldn&#x27;t be astounded by what these Ai agents can do as of today, but here I am still amazed.<p>I&#x27;ve even got support from a Sim racing guy and built a web driver so he gets full force feedback for his rig, and it works.<p>Anyway, just a bit of fun!<p>Uses LIDAR data from the UK Gov + OpenStreetMap data to build the world. Technically, I could do the whole of England&#x2F;Wales...but the data storage would be huge!", "title": "Show HN: Drive around my village in 3D", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:55:21Z", "url": "https://cherwellvalleymotorclub.app"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "dannyboland"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Building a wireless network adapter for the Super Nintendo"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://boland.dev/snet/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_dannyboland", "story_50611861", "front_page"], "author": "dannyboland", "children": [50614063, 50614778, 50614949, 50615377, 50615435, 50616163, 50616875], "created_at": "2026-11-23T14:16:37Z", "created_at_i": 1795443397, "num_comments": 10, "objectID": "50611861", "points": 42, "story_id": 50611861, "title": "Building a wireless network adapter for the Super Nintendo", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:55:51Z", "url": "https://boland.dev/snet/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "evakhoury"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Let's Meet in the Middle"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://george.mand.is/2026/11/lets-meet-in-the-middle/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_evakhoury", "story_50577534", "front_page"], "author": "evakhoury", "children": [50615854, 50616651, 50617068], "created_at": "2026-11-20T16:41:54Z", "created_at_i": 1795192914, "num_comments": 4, "objectID": "50577534", "points": 41, "story_id": 50577534, "title": "Let's Meet in the Middle", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:57:19Z", "url": "https://george.mand.is/2026/11/lets-meet-in-the-middle/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "MrBuddyCasino"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Dario is hyping the dangers so OSS models are illegal and *he* stays in control"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://twitter.com/ylecun/status/2124550037912920090"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_MrBuddyCasino", "story_50615308", "front_page"], "author": "MrBuddyCasino", "children": [50616690, 50616703, 50616911], "created_at": "2026-11-23T17:07:26Z", "created_at_i": 1795453646, "num_comments": 7, "objectID": "50615308", "points": 36, "story_id": 50615308, "title": "Dario is hyping the dangers so OSS models are illegal and *he* stays in control", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:57:19Z", "url": "https://twitter.com/ylecun/status/2124550037912920090"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "lawik"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Reviving the Donkey Car with Erlang"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://underjord.io/reviving-the-donkey-car-with-erlang.html"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_lawik", "story_50583535", "front_page"], "author": "lawik", "children": [50614193, 50615043], "created_at": "2026-11-20T22:56:20Z", "created_at_i": 1795215380, "num_comments": 1, "objectID": "50583535", "points": 34, "story_id": 50583535, "title": "Reviving the Donkey Car with Erlang", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:31:00Z", "url": "https://underjord.io/reviving-the-donkey-car-with-erlang.html"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "toebee"}, "story_text": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "We built NariQ: 3-bit-or-lower quantizations of Qwen3.8-27B that retain near-BF16 quality across agentic tasks, math, multilingual reasoning, and image understanding.<p>To our knowledge, this is the first 3-bit-or-lower quantization that retains BF16 lvl performance on long-horizon agentic tasks.<p>Benchmarks (BF16 / 3-bit / 2.5-bit / 2-bit):<p>- DeepSWE: 39.8 / 41.0 / 41.9 / 28.6<p>- Terminal-Bench 2.1: 62.6 / 63.8 / 60.2 / 52.4<p>- AIME 25+26: 97.7 / 98.3 / 96.5 / 86.0<p>- MSGM: 94.0 / 93.1 / 91.8 / 90.6<p>- RealWorldQA: 82.4 / 82.4 / 81.3 / 80.9<p>Decode speed is comparable to other quants on an RTX PRO 6000. Context-length results below<p>(3-bit / 2.5-bit / 2-bit / Unsloth UD-IQ3_XXS):<p>- 4K: 88.9 / 99.2 / 111.7 / 94.7<p>- 16K: 84.5 / 93.8 / 105.1 / 89.8<p>- 64K: 70.7 / 77.5 / 85.0 / 74.8<p>Running these currently require our llama.cpp fork:\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/nari-labs/nari-llama.cpp\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/nari-labs/nari-llama.cpp</a>)<p>Feedback and questions welcome. We'd love to hear how these perform on your workloads."}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "NariQ: BF16-level Qwen3.8-27B in a 10 GB file"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://huggingface.co/nari-labs/Qwen3.8-27B-NariQ-GGUF"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_toebee", "story_50611402", "front_page"], "author": "toebee", "children": [50611403, 50611442], "created_at": "2026-11-23T13:42:38Z", "created_at_i": 1795441358, "num_comments": 0, "objectID": "50611402", "points": 11, "story_id": 50611402, "story_text": "We built NariQ: 3-bit-or-lower quantizations of Qwen3.8-27B that retain near-BF16 quality across agentic tasks, math, multilingual reasoning, and image understanding.<p>To our knowledge, this is the first 3-bit-or-lower quantization that retains BF16 lvl performance on long-horizon agentic tasks.<p>Benchmarks (BF16 &#x2F; 3-bit &#x2F; 2.5-bit &#x2F; 2-bit):<p>- DeepSWE: 39.8 &#x2F; 41.0 &#x2F; 41.9 &#x2F; 28.6<p>- Terminal-Bench 2.1: 62.6 &#x2F; 63.8 &#x2F; 60.2 &#x2F; 52.4<p>- AIME 25+26: 97.7 &#x2F; 98.3 &#x2F; 96.5 &#x2F; 86.0<p>- MSGM: 94.0 &#x2F; 93.1 &#x2F; 91.8 &#x2F; 90.6<p>- RealWorldQA: 82.4 &#x2F; 82.4 &#x2F; 81.3 &#x2F; 80.9<p>Decode speed is comparable to other quants on an RTX PRO 6000. Context-length results below<p>(3-bit &#x2F; 2.5-bit &#x2F; 2-bit &#x2F; Unsloth UD-IQ3_XXS):<p>- 4K: 88.9 &#x2F; 99.2 &#x2F; 111.7 &#x2F; 94.7<p>- 16K: 84.5 &#x2F; 93.8 &#x2F; 105.1 &#x2F; 89.8<p>- 64K: 70.7 &#x2F; 77.5 &#x2F; 85.0 &#x2F; 74.8<p>Running these currently require our llama.cpp fork:\n(<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;nari-labs&#x2F;nari-llama.cpp\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;github.com&#x2F;nari-labs&#x2F;nari-llama.cpp</a>)<p>Feedback and questions welcome. We&#x27;d love to hear how these perform on your workloads.", "title": "NariQ: BF16-level Qwen3.8-27B in a 10 GB file", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:57:19Z", "url": "https://huggingface.co/nari-labs/Qwen3.8-27B-NariQ-GGUF"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "dakshgupta"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "How should an LLM see a computer?"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://www.greptile.com/blog/trex-computer-use"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_dakshgupta", "story_50615520", "front_page"], "author": "dakshgupta", "children": [50616779, 50616838, 50616867, 50616888, 50617063], "created_at": "2026-11-23T17:19:25Z", "created_at_i": 1795454365, "num_comments": 6, "objectID": "50615520", "points": 9, "story_id": 50615